Package: PaleoMapR
Type: Package
Title: Point-and-Click Editor for Fossil-Corrected Paleogeographic Maps
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Michiel", family = "Arts", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "michiel.arts@stratigraphy.eu", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3181-4608"))
Description: Opens a 'shiny' application in the web browser that checks the
    PALEOMAP paleodigital elevation models (Scotese and Wright (2018)
    <https://www.earthbyte.org/paleodem-resource-scotese-and-wright-2018/>)
    against fossil collections from the Paleobiology Database, rock units from
    Macrostrat (Peters et al. (2018) <doi:10.1029/2018GC007467>) and the
    user's own points, and rebuilds fossil-corrected elevation grids in which
    marine records lie in the sea and terrestrial records on land, starting
    from the paleocoastlines of Kocsis and Scotese (2021)
    <doi:10.1016/j.earscirev.2020.103463>. Publication maps of the corrected
    grids are drawn as PNG and vector PDF in many projections, as whole maps,
    zoomed-in areas or composites, with localities and with climate layers
    from the HadCM3L simulations of Valdes et al. (2021)
    <doi:10.5194/cp-17-1483-2021>. Plate rotations use 'pyGPlates' (Mueller
    et al. (2018) <doi:10.1029/2018GC007584>) through 'reticulate'. Points,
    edits and settings are plain text files in a working folder.
License: GPL (>= 2)
